I cound't help myself and did another coding challange. Here's the task:
"Given a string, determine whether the number of vowels in the first half of the string is equal to the number of vowels in the second half.

The string can contain any characters.
The letters a, e, i, o, and u, in either uppercase or lowercase, are considered vowels.
If there's an odd number of characters in the string, ignore the center character."

First I converted every character in s to lowercase. Then I get the middle of s using "len(s) // 2" and stored it in the variable "mid".
I checked if the string in s was an even or an odd number and depending on that sliced it accordingly. I created two variables for the first and the second
half of the string. Using a for-loop I checked for the vowels in each half and stored the numbers in variabls I created earlier. Then I compared the number
in each variable and if it was eqal, it returned True.
